# Solventa tests

These rules live with the Android app and apply only to tests under `apps/mobile/`. Do not use them for `apps/web/` or `apps/backend/`.

From the wiki: [Estrategia de pruebas §4.3](https://github.com/martin-hendricks/MISO-PROYECTO-FINAL-SOLVENTA/wiki/Estrategia-de-pruebas#43-framework-para-el-componente-móvil) and [§2.6](https://github.com/martin-hendricks/MISO-PROYECTO-FINAL-SOLVENTA/wiki/Estrategia-de-pruebas#26-patrones-y-lineamientos-de-automatización).

- JVM unit tests live in `app/src/test` and run with `./gradlew :app:testDebugUnitTest` from `apps/mobile/Solventa`. Cover ViewModel state, domain use cases, and `*RepositoryImpl` (Retrofit to `bff-movil` vs Room). No emulator.
- A ViewModel test fakes the use case. It does not call Retrofit or Room. An offline-evidence test belongs on the repository: failed network, encrypted Room row, WorkManager queue, idempotent replay.
- Compose UI and E2E tests live in `app/src/androidTest` and use `createAndroidComposeRule`. Name the scenario Given / When / Then.
- Find nodes with semantics or `testTag`. Do not use xpath, css, or `Thread.sleep`.
- Locale tests set `LocalConfiguration` to `es-CO`, `es-MX`, `es-CL`, and `es-PE` and assert copy plus `NumberFormat` / `DateFormat`.

```kotlin
@Test
fun givenPolicies_whenHomeLoads_thenShowsEmpty() {
    val viewModel = HomeViewModel(FakeLoadPolicies())
    assertEquals(UiState.Ready(emptyList()), viewModel.state.value)
}
```
